cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper below."
type: software
title: "CRANE: Counterfactual Retrieval via Agnostic Nearest-neighbour Explanations"
abstract: >
  CRANE is a Python library for generating post-hoc, model-agnostic
  nearest-neighbour counterfactual explanations for multimodal classifiers.
  It supports tabular, time-series, text, and image modalities, including
  multiple named branches of the same modality type, and provides unimodal
  generators (TabularNN, TimeSeriesNN, TextNN, ImageNN) as well as
  multimodal retrieval strategies: Early-Fusion Nearest Neighbour (EF-NN),
  Intermediate-Fusion Nearest Neighbour (IF-NN), Multimodal Consensus
  Retrieval (MC-R), and Modality-wise Prototype Synthesis (MPS). Candidates
  are evaluated against four objectives: outcome, proximity, sparsity, and
  plausibility.
